    "body": "With a `GPTModelProvider`, `mtp_num_layers > 0`, and `dist.use_decentralized_pg=True`, model construction reaches MCore's global pipeline-rank fallback even though Bridge has already supplied the provider's process-group collection. The global MPU pipeline group is unset in that mode, so MTP spec construction fails before training starts.\n\nForward the rank from the provider's pipeline group to the final `get_gpt_mtp_block_spec` call. This completes the Bridge caller migration started in #5752: its decoder callable receives `pp_rank`, but the final MTP helper still omitted it. Calls without a provider process-group collection retain their existing fallback. There are no public signature, dependency, or submodule changes.\n\nThe supported path is Bridge pretrain/setup → decentralized initialization → `ModelProviderMixin.get_model` → `GPTModelProvider.provide` → `mtp_block_spec`. This change is scoped to that provider path; it does not claim validation of all decentralized distributed training combinations.\n\nValidation uses Bridge base `9166429859ed9a29860ca2e1f3fc317173df8c0e` and its exact MCore pin `8949def81eb744b9219e2d794c80265928c40a5b`. MCore discovery base was `b86e75c184483a54689d17b1a9eb6c5bcc999425`; a later default-branch recheck observed `6a6c8aa6e9ee258db08bed381e882c0f754d14bc`, which does not change the pinned test dependency.\n\n- Red, with only the new regression applied to unchanged production code: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/models/test_gpt_provider.py -k test_mtp_spec_uses_provider_pipeline_group -q -p no:cacheprovider` — exit 1, all three cases fail with `AssertionError: MTP spec must not read global pipeline rank`. The test calls the real pinned MCore spec builder; it covers PP=1 and both PP=2 ranks.\n- Green, identical command after the fix — exit 0, 3 passed.\n- Adjacent: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/models/test_gpt_provider.py tests/unit_tests/models/test_model_provider_mixin.py -q -p no:cacheprovider` — exit 0, 45 passed, 1 existing GPU-dependent test skipped.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` — exit 0; no files modified.\n- Supplemental `uv run mypy --strict src/megatron/bridge/models/gpt_provider.py` — mypy 2.2.0 exits 2 with the same internal tool error on both the unmodified base and patched source. No passing type-check result is claimed.\n\nValidation is CPU contract coverage, not a GPU training result. A separate read-only review of the final diff, source ownership, duplicate search, supported path, and red/green evidence found no blocking findings. All-state searches in both repositories found related upstream caller work in NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#8048 and fallback changes in NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#8057, but neither updates this Bridge call.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
